  "settingsSelectTodayShiftFromPattern": "Select today's shift from the pattern",
  "settingsScheduleChangeWarning": "Existing alarms will be deleted, and 10 days of alarms will be generated for the new schedule.",
  "settingsResetScheduleConfirm": "Reset your shift schedule and all alarms?\n(The full team schedule will also be reset.)",
  "settingsHelpRefreshCycleTitle": "Alarm Refresh Cycle",
  "settingsHelpRefreshCycleDesc": "When you first register alarms, 10 days' worth are created at once.\n\nAfter that, one more day is added automatically every midnight, so 10 days of alarms are always kept ready.\n\nThis refresh happens automatically in the background, even if you don't open the app.",
  "settingsHelpChangeShiftTitle": "Changing Shifts from the Calendar",
  "settingsHelpChangeShiftDesc": "Long-press a date on the calendar to change that day's shift.\n\n• Irregular workers: assign a shift directly to any date\n• Regular workers: change just a specific date to a different shift\n\nWhen you change a shift, the alarms for that date update automatically.",
  "settingsHelpTeamChangeTitle": "How to Apply a Team Change",
  "settingsHelpTeamChangeDesc": "When your team changes and you need to update your whole schedule:\n\nGo to Settings → the Edit button on the Manage Shift Work card → select \"Change Schedule.\"\n\nSelect today's shift based on your new team, and it will apply to the whole calendar, with 10 days of alarms newly generated.\n\n※ If the shift pattern itself changes (e.g. going from a 3-team/2-shift rotation to a 4-team/3-shift rotation), you'll need to reset instead - in that case all existing alarms are deleted.",
  "settingsHelpDataStorageTitle": "Data Storage Info",
  "settingsHelpDataStorageDesc": "All data stored by the app (alarms, memos, shift schedule) is kept only on your local device.\n\n• It is never sent to an external server, and only you can access it.\n• Deleting the app deletes all data with it.\n• Updating the app keeps your data intact.\n\nIf you need a backup, please save your data separately.",
  "settingsPrivacyPolicyBody": "Shiftbell Privacy Policy\n\n1. Personal Information We Collect\nThis app does not collect personal information. All data (shift schedule, alarm settings, etc.) is stored only on your device and is never transmitted to an external server.\n\n2. App Permissions\n• Display over other apps: Needed to show the alarm screen while you're using other apps.\n• Notifications: Needed to show pre-alarm notifications and alarm status.\n\n3. Data Storage\nAll data is stored only on your device. Deleting the app deletes all data with it.\n\n4. Contact\nlowvibe07.tistory.com\n\nLast updated: December 2025",
